VALUES ('“I want to be a jockey like Wesley”', 'i-want-to-be-a-jockey-like-wesley', '<p><strong><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Iss-75-Front-Cover-212x300.png" alt="" width="212" height="300" srcset="https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Iss-75-Front-Cover-212x300.png 212w, https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Iss-75-Front-Cover-724x1024.png 724w, https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Iss-75-Front-Cover.png 764w" sizes="(max-width: 212px) 100vw, 212px" />Where are you from?</strong></p>
<p>&#8220;My name is John Wyse and I’m 11 years old and I’m from Ballynanty in Limerick.&#8221;</p>
<p><strong>Why do you like Monty so much? What is Monty like?</strong></p>
<p>&#8220;Monty is a hard pony to hold. He’s a good pony and I like him cause he’s quiet but very fast.<br />
I like all the ponies &#8211; we have six now. I really like Comet too&#8230; I’ll be riding Comet in future. Tianna &#8211; she’s my age too &#8211; and she rides Comet.&#8221;</p>
<p><strong>How often do you meet Monty?</strong></p>
<p>&#8220;We go to the stables every week, more often when we’re on our holidays from school.&#8221;</p>
<p><strong>What do you do when you go to the stables?</strong></p>
<p>&#8220;I groom all the horses, then go for a cup of tea, then we go riding&#8221;</p>
<p><strong>How long are you going to the stables?</strong></p>
<p>&#8220;About two years I think. My brothers used to go and I went with them one day to meet the bus. I was on my bike and was going to cycle back home, but I asked Karen could I go too. Next thing I was on the bus with my bike too.&#8221;</p>
<p><strong>Who else goes to the stables with you?</strong></p>
<p>&#8220;I go with my two bothers Jordan and Michael and other people in my group.&#8221;<br />
<strong>What do you want to do when you grow up?</strong></p>
<p>&#8220;I want to be a jockey like Wesley!&#8221;</p>
<figure aria-describedby="caption-attachment-251416"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Karen-Keehan-youth-worker-with-MYA.png" alt="" width="1542" height="873" srcset="https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Karen-Keehan-youth-worker-with-MYA.png 1542w, https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Karen-Keehan-youth-worker-with-MYA-300x170.png 300w, https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Karen-Keehan-youth-worker-with-MYA-1024x580.png 1024w, https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Karen-Keehan-youth-worker-with-MYA-768x435.png 768w, https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Karen-Keehan-youth-worker-with-MYA-1536x870.png 1536w, https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Karen-Keehan-youth-worker-with-MYA-1080x611.png 1080w" sizes="(max-width: 1542px) 100vw, 1542px" /><figcaption><em>• Our thanks to youth worker Karen Keehan (pictured above) for interviewing John. She always makes a good impression on young people in the area. Her willingness to connect is apparent in these &#8216;Changing Ireland&#8217; photos taken in Sarsfield Gardens, Moyross, in 2015.<br /></em></figcaption></figure>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Youth-worker-Karen-Keehan-watches-a-novice-sulky-rider-in-Sarsfield-Gardens-Moyross.jpg" alt="" width="2256" height="1504" srcset="https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Youth-worker-Karen-Keehan-watches-a-novice-sulky-rider-in-Sarsfield-Gardens-Moyross.jpg 2256w, https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Youth-worker-Karen-Keehan-watches-a-novice-sulky-rider-in-Sarsfield-Gardens-Moyross-300x200.jpg 300w, https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Youth-worker-Karen-Keehan-watches-a-novice-sulky-rider-in-Sarsfield-Gardens-Moyross-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Youth-worker-Karen-Keehan-watches-a-novice-sulky-rider-in-Sarsfield-Gardens-Moyross-768x512.jpg 768w, https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Youth-worker-Karen-Keehan-watches-a-novice-sulky-rider-in-Sarsfield-Gardens-Moyross-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Youth-worker-Karen-Keehan-watches-a-novice-sulky-rider-in-Sarsfield-Gardens-Moyross-2048x1365.jpg 2048w, https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Youth-worker-Karen-Keehan-watches-a-novice-sulky-rider-in-Sarsfield-Gardens-Moyross-1080x720.jpg 1080w" sizes="(max-width: 2256px) 100vw, 2256px" /></p>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Karen-Keehan-on-a-sulky-outside-our-office-in-2015.jpg" alt="" width="2256" height="1504" srcset="https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Karen-Keehan-on-a-sulky-outside-our-office-in-2015.jpg 2256w, https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Karen-Keehan-on-a-sulky-outside-our-office-in-2015-300x200.jpg 300w, https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Karen-Keehan-on-a-sulky-outside-our-office-in-2015-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Karen-Keehan-on-a-sulky-outside-our-office-in-2015-768x512.jpg 768w, https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Karen-Keehan-on-a-sulky-outside-our-office-in-2015-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Karen-Keehan-on-a-sulky-outside-our-office-in-2015-2048x1365.jpg 2048w, https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Karen-Keehan-on-a-sulky-outside-our-office-in-2015-1080x720.jpg 1080w" sizes="(max-width: 2256px) 100vw, 2256px" /></p>
<p><strong>Read our article about Moyross&#8217;s healthy obsession with horse-riding, the benefits of youthwork and the success of locally-born jockey Wesley Joyce (below).<br />
</strong></p>
<p><strong>For more information about Moyross Youth Academy, contact:</strong><br />
Andrew O’Byrne on 085 853 0463 or at andrew@mya.irish<br />
Elaine Slattery on 087 283 5390 or at elaine@mya.irish</p>
<blockquote><p><a href="https://changingireland.ie/moyross-where-every-youngster-backs-wesley/">Moyross &#8211; where every youngster backs Wesley!</a></p></blockquote>
<p><iframe sandbox="allow-scripts" security="restricted" title="“Moyross – where every youngster backs Wesley!” — Changing Ireland" src="https://changingireland.ie/moyross-where-every-youngster-backs-wesley/embed/#?secret=CPRTllihM3#?secret=3fHKd1omib" width="600" height="338" frameborder="0" marginwidth="0" marginheight="0" scrolling="no"></iframe></p>', 'John Wyse (11) and his favourite horse Monty feature on the front cover of our latest edition. John was interviewed by Karen Keehan, a youth worker with Moyross Youth Academy.', 'https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Monty-is-so-comfortable-with-John-its-lovely-to-see-this-bond-developing-says-MYA-scaled.jpg', '', '[{"slug":"education-training","title":"Education & Training"},{"slug":"empowerment","title":"Empowerment"}]', '[]', '', 251411, 1, '2022-01-13T12:00:16Z', '2022-01-13T16:07:07Z', '2022-01-13T12:00:16Z')
